A||||9||filthyscarecrow||anyone else have this problem?||||1||
Z||000000||filthyscarecrow||11-09-2001||01:26 PM||||okay, i have my dad's car (86SE), and ever since he's owned it, it's jerked. its' a really weird condition, it only jerks at constant throttle adn low rpm. so like 30mph in 3rd gear (4spd) it jerks like crazy. the repair shop told him to change the ECM, but he didn't have a spare. i do, but i figured i'd ask before i go messin with stuff... <BR>they also said leaky injectors, but i chnaged them with the inj/rail from my 85GT and it didn't solve anything. i'm really clueless on this one. anyone have any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Voytek||11-09-2001||02:33 PM||||Has anything else been changed on this engine?  Like spark plug wires?  I've had 1 or 2 faulty wires once and you couldn't tell visually.  The engine just wasn't getting the spark and it would jerk at low throttle.  At high throttle, the car actually ran good because the spark would 'jump' the wire break.  Anyway, this is low cost maintenance if you haven't already done this.  BTW, my wires were fairly new, too.  Could be the short wire between the distributor and ignition.<P>Other than that, maybe a bad plug.  I've seen a cracked one (not on a Fiero).  I don't know why it was cracked by it sort of worked at high throttle and wasn't doing much at low throttle.<P>I would consider the ECM to be a last ditch effort.  I've owned 5 Fieros (6 total in the family).  I've had just about everything replaced (between all the cars) but NEVER the ECM.<P>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||11-09-2001||02:56 PM||||a minivan i bought last year did that, it was only a bad coil pack. It may be at that 'sweet spot' where the trans is searching for the right gear too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||11-09-2001||04:37 PM||||My 86 GT does the same thing, at a constant low speed little or no throttle.  Runs fine when giving it thottle.  Cause unknown but interested in a cure.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000004||reddog||11-10-2001||01:23 AM||||Ditto, I suspect that it's either the distributor,leaking or bad injectors, or timing chain stretched beyond specs. Have also heard that a bad tach filter could cause similar problems.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||filthyscarecrow||11-10-2001||01:33 AM||||well, i put new plugs, wires, adn coil on it this spring (all needed to be replaced anyway) and it didn't fix it. like i said before, the injectors werent' the problem becasue i changed them too. i'm thinkin maybe distributor or timing chain now. thanks for the help...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Yorgo||11-12-2001||10:20 PM||||I had the exact same symptoms.  Turned out to be a faulty throttle position sensor.  Replaced it and the problem was gone.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Countach||11-13-2001||01:37 AM||||That last suggestion sounds pretty good, T.P.S., another I'd try after that would be motor/tranny mounts. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||11-13-2001||10:03 AM||||That automatic Idle control sensor does sound like it could be failing.  I had a similar problem where it would idle or go like a bat out of hell, but if you tried to drive around town, it would start to buck and die. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  It turned out to ALSO be my fuel pump was bad. (ok, who put in the aftermarket one?)<BR>I don't think my sensors were in great shape either.  2 cents....ching ching. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||K2m4||11-13-2001||11:25 AM||||I would say it was the Throttle position sensor. Remove and and push the lever with your finger and see if you can feel a flat spot on the coil inside. Replacing that on my 4 banger cured a world of problems with bucking at a contant throttle position.<P>kerm<BR>86 GT<BR>86 2M4<BR>||||reg||1
